# Spiral in Livebook

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:spiral_kino, path: Path.join(__DIR__, "..")}
])
```

## Running Spiral

Insert a cell with **+ Smart → Spiral**. Write Spiral code in the editor; the form above it
picks the backend, the timeout and whether to show the generated code. The cell compiles
and runs the code through the Spiral .NET Interactive kernel (the polyglot fork of
`dotnet repl`); program output, the value of the last expression and compile errors show
up in the cell.

The default backend compiles to F# and evaluates it, showing the value of the last
expression:

<!-- livebook:{"attrs":{"backend":"fsharp","builder_args":"","print_code":false,"source":"inl square x = x * x\n\nconsole.write_line \"Hello from Spiral!\"\nsquare 7i32\n","timeout":300},"chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.Spiral.Kino.SmartCell","livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
Spiral.Kino.eval!(
  ~S"""
  inl square x = x * x

  console.write_line "Hello from Spiral!"
  square 7i32
  """,
  timeout: 300000
)
```

With **Show generated code** the generated F# is printed before the program output:

<!-- livebook:{"attrs":{"backend":"fsharp","builder_args":"","print_code":true,"source":"inl fib (n : i32) : i32 =\n    let rec loop (a : i32) (b : i32) (n : i32) : i32 =\n        if n <= 0 then a else loop b (a + b) (n - 1)\n    loop 0 1 n\n\nfib 20\n","timeout":300},"chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.Spiral.Kino.SmartCell","livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
Spiral.Kino.eval!(
  ~S"""
  inl fib (n : i32) : i32 =
      let rec loop (a : i32) (b : i32) (n : i32) : i32 =
          if n <= 0 then a else loop b (a + b) (n - 1)
      loop 0 1 n

  fib 20
  """,
  timeout: 300000,
  print_code: true
)
```

Other backends are selected in the form (or with `///>` lines in the code). Builder backends
report the output of the generated program:

<!-- livebook:{"attrs":{"backend":"lua","builder_args":"","print_code":false,"source":"console.write_line \"Hello from Lua!\"\n","timeout":300},"chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.Spiral.Kino.SmartCell","livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
Spiral.Kino.eval!(
  ~S"""
  console.write_line "Hello from Lua!"
  """,
  backend: "lua",
  timeout: 300000
)
```

Directives can also be written directly in the code; they are merged with the form
options. Only the first `///-` line is read by the kernel, and every `///>` line adds a
backend. A `////>` line is disabled.

## Programmatic use

`Spiral.Kino.run/2` returns a `Spiral.Kino.Result` instead of rendering:

```elixir
{:ok, result} = Spiral.Kino.run("1i32 + 2i32", timeout: 120_000)
result.value
```

## Errors

Compile errors are raised as `Spiral.Kino.SpiralError` (positions refer to the kernel's
wrapped `main.spi`):

<!-- livebook:{"attrs":{"backend":"fsharp","builder_args":"","print_code":false,"source":"1i32 + \"a\"\n","timeout":300},"chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.Spiral.Kino.SmartCell","livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
Spiral.Kino.eval!(
  ~S"""
  1i32 + "a"
  """,
  timeout: 300000
)
```
